			<div class="content" id="post-content-1445614">
									

<p>Because there is a <em>reason</em> to destroy 682: it's objectively massively dangerous.</p>
<p>1129 hasn't displayed any forms of aggression or danger except that the people affected by it desperately want to destroy it. It doesn't present any direct threat except for the feeling that it's &quot;wrong&quot;.</p>
<p>As for why the researchers aren't requesting flamethrowers, etc., remember that the people's cognitive skills aren't impaired. They just have the need/compulsion to destroy this at the forefront. And someone with more information on this thing (like the researchers would), knows that to face it directly <em>won't work</em>. So they're trying to find more indirect means to destroy it.</p>

