			<div class="content" id="post-content-1455309">
									

<p>I just re-read and realized my mistake. There is no actual threat, it just exists in a fundamentally disconcerting way and provokes emotional responses. My brain tacked on some physical danger apparantly drawn from thin air. Hmmmm, maybe I'm falling under Stage 2 effects?</p>
<p>Also, that is a very interesting point about the researchers destruction methods. It makes a lot of sense. But the description of stage 2 implies that they can not be dissuaded and will continue to pursue destruction unless made to forget that 1129 exists. Flamethrowers and grenades mgiht not be the prefered strategy, but they wouldn't let a rubber-stamp decomission rejection stop their efforts. I picture this conversation:</p>
<p>Exposed Researcher 1: The O5s rejected our proposal for 1129.<br />
Exposed Researcher 2: Those fools! Can't they see how dangerous it is!<br />
ER1: I know, right?!?<br />
ER2: Dammit, well we knew this was a possibility. On to Plan B.<br />
ER1: *sigh* I was hoping it wouldn't come to this. I've got a drum of napalm already hooked up to the sprinkler system in that wing. Let's flip a coin to see who has to start the trash-can fire.<br />
ER2: heads!</p>

